  <prompt>Decide and build how each customer gets its own Copilot agent bound to its own BFF.</prompt>

  <goal>
    A design (facts, one recommendation) and then the provisioning step for a per-customer M365 Copilot agent:
    where the package lives (Model 1 users are guests in Spaarke's tenant, so one app catalog holds every customer's agent),
    how it reaches the customer's BFF (its own scope, pre-authorization by H3), who can see it (the customer's security
    group), and how it is updated.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>src/solutions/CopilotAgent is an M365 declarative-agent / Teams package deployed by scripts/Deploy-CopilotAgent.ps1;
      it is not Dataverse content, so it is not part of SpaarkeMaster (T218).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/solutions/CopilotAgent/**; scripts/Deploy-CopilotAgent.ps1</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/t240-plan.md (shared clients, directory)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

